<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Image with Caption</title>
  <style>
    body {
      display: flex;
      justify-content: center;
      align-items: center;
      height: 100vh;
      margin: 0;
      background-color: #f0f0f0;
    }

    .img-container {
      text-align: center;
    }

    .img-container img {
      width: 100%;
      max-height: 500px; /* Adjust based on your image size */
      object-fit: cover;
      border-radius: 8px;
    }

    .img-container p {
      margin-top: 20px;
      font-size: 16px;
      color: #777;
      opacity: 0.8;
      text-shadow: 2px 2px 4px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5);
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="img-container">
  <a href="http://www.example.com" target="_blank">
    <img src="image.jpg" alt="Image">
  </a>
  <p>Caption goes here</p>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### Explanation:

1. **Flexbox Layout**: The `.img-container` div uses Flexbox to center the image both horizontally and vertically within the container.

2. **Image Styling**:
   - `width: 100%` ensures the image covers the full width of its parent container.
   - `max-height: 500px` (adjustable) sets the maximum height of the image while maintaining its aspect ratio using `object-fit: cover`. This helps prevent images from being distorted when resized.

3. **Caption Styling**: 
   - The caption has a top margin to separate it from the image.
   - A light gray shadow (`text-shadow`) gives the caption a subtle depth effect.
   - `opacity: 0.8` makes the caption semi-transparent, enhancing readability.

